t worked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the far end of a shaft — does not. It is read only for a verb the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"game"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" invented. A row reclaiming a built-in or a stub reclaims that"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"verb’s answer and not its physics, so the standard table’s column","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stands: ","type":"text"},{"code":"take","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has to reach what it takes whoever writes the sentence.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to acknowledge that this row reclaims a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"built-in’s stage-4 default. See "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/action(_:reach:overriding:perform:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"overriding"},{"name":"line","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sentence.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The intent action.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StubVerbs"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is what "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"action(.wind) { try reply(Prose.cannotWind) }"},{"type":"text","text":" was reaching"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for, and it is not the same thing. A closure runs whatever it was written"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to run; a line takes the path a stub verb takes, which renders the object’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name, agrees with its number and answers "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wind me"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wind the troll"},{"type":"text","text":" in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the engine’s own words. The reach guard is not the difference any more:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"both forms declare it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reach:"},{"type":"text","text":", and a custom intent has no column"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anywhere else — it is in neither half of the standard table, so without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wind the clock"},{"type":"text","text":" through the glass of a shut cabinet answers as though"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the player were holding it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var actions: [IntentAction] {","    action(.wind, reach: .directObject, say: Prose.verbWindNothing)","    action(.temple, say: Prose.graniteWordInert)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The line is a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"floor"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", not a refusal. It is spoken with "},{"code":"say","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"reply","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", exactly as a stub verb’s is, so "},{"code":"after","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" rules still get their turn"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the world clock advances — winding a clock that will not wind still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes time. Anything that wants to answer "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"instead","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" promotes itself the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ordinary way, in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"before","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rule.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This form names nothing, so it is the one for a verb whose sentence never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mentions what the player pointed at. Where the sentence does, use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/action(_:reach:overriding:naming:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which hands the line the object’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rendered name and answers ","type":"text"},{"code":"wind me","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"wind the troll","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the engine’s own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"words.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Choosing this form for a verb whose rows carry a "},{"code":".directObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"choice, and it has a cost."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The engine forbids the same shape in its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"table — "},{"code":"StubVerb.namesObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the "},{"code":"everyStubWithAnObjectSlotCanNameIt","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"test are #245 — because a line that cannot say what the player pointed at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"looks correct from both sides and is wrong from neither. A game is allowed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, because a game may be reproducing a source whose answer is genuinely"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nameless: Zork’s "},{"code":"V-WIND","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is “You cannot wind up a X.” and "},{"code":"Sources\/Zork1\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declines the reproduction for a reason it writes down. What you are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepting is that the sentence is aimed at the player too — "},{"code":"ring me","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"answers whatever "},{"code":"ring the bell","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" answers, where a "},{"code":"naming:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" line would have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"said "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/StubReplies\/yourself","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". Take the cost knowingly or take the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other form."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sentence is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":" and not a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Line","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", which is the type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the engine’s own stub lines are held in, and the difference is deliberate:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Line"},{"type":"text","text":" is not convertible from a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":" constant, so every row would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"say: .init(Prose.cannotWind)"},{"type":"text","text":" to say what "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"say: Prose.cannotWind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"says. The one thing the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Line"},{"type":"text","text":" spelling would add is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Line\/live(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — a nameless sentence assembled when it prints —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the closure form already covers that with more power, since it runs in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the live turn frame rather than being handed nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/action(_:reach:overriding:say:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Intent":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Intent","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Intent","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/intent","kind":"symbol","title":"Intent","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A canonical action the player can attempt. Games can mint their own —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most readably with "},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or directly ("},{"code":"Intent(\"ring\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") — and register"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verbs and default behavior for them."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Intent"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/action(_:reach:overriding:say:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A custom verb’s own default line: the sentence it answers with when no rule","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"of the game’s has anything better to say.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/action(_:reach:overriding:say:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"action"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto6IntentV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Intent"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"reach","kind":"ex